# The General Court lane, one step per line, run in order by watchers/gc_lane.py.
# A step is what follows "python3". "handover " in front means the step takes
# archive/.lock itself. A line is run once; logs/gc_lane.done lists what has run.
# Add a step only once its fetcher has been read for the one-worker rules.

# 2015-2016: the 883 bills the database's Docket view does not reach (it
# stops part way through 2016). Its 905 covered bills are seeded, never asked.
fetch_archive_docket.py --term 2015-2016 --seed Docket_db_2015-2016.txt --delay 15 --stop-refused 2

# 2015-2016 again, with the seed corrected. The database's "2016" is not 2016:
# its 1,962 SessionYear-2016 rows are all dated 2015, the first-year history
# of 190 bills carried over, and two of them carry another bill's LSR. So the
# step above skips 190 bills whose whole 2016 record is missing. This seed
# (Docket_db_2015.txt) keeps only session-2015 rows of bills data/bills.json
# files under 2015, with the bill's own LSR: 8,322 rows on 716 bills. Every
# one of the 1,072 bills filed under 2016 then comes from its own page; the
# 883 above are cached, so this asks for the other 189 and rewrites the file.
fetch_archive_docket.py --term 2015-2016 --seed Docket_db_2015.txt --delay 15 --stop-refused 2
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-docket

# BILL TEXT, 1989-2024: 31,003 requests by --plan, one per bill, 15s apart.
# Bounded runs of 800 with an hour's rest between. A proving run first, on
# the static path, where 96 of 96 sampled House and Senate bills served.
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2021 --to 2021 --kinds HB,SB --budget 20 --note proving
watchers/rest.py 1800 after-proving
# 2017-2021, static: 4,280.
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-a
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-a
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-b
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-b
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-c
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-c
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-d
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-d
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-e
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-e
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2017 --to 2021 --budget 800 --note 2017-21-f
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2017-21-f
# 2023-2024, the application, stored id with sy: 1,996. A short run first,
# so the LSR check meets the application's pages before it meets 800 of them.
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2023 --to 2024 --budget 25 --note 2023-24-proving
watchers/rest.py 1800 after-2023-24-proving
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2023 --to 2024 --budget 800 --note 2023-24-a
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2023-24-a
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2023 --to 2024 --budget 800 --note 2023-24-b
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2023-24-b
fetch_legislation.py --all --from 2023 --to 2024 --budget 800 --note 2023-24-c
watchers/rest.py 3600 after-2023-24-c
